The Giant Mole is accessed by digging with a [[spade]] on top of the [[mole hill]]s in the [[Falador Park]]. A [[light source]] is required to navigate the tunnels without taking damage. [[Candle]]s, [[torch]]es, or [[oil lamp]]s will be extinguished if it retreats within [[melee]] range. A [[tinderbox]] is needed to relight extinguished light sources. 

Completion of [[Making Friends With My Arm]] unlocks the ability to create the [[Fire of Eternal Light]] within the lair, which acts as a permanent unextinguishable light source in the tunnels.

==Fight overview==
{{Main|Giant Mole/Strategies}}
[[File:Fighting the Giant Mole.png|thumb|left|250px|A player fights the Giant Mole, the result of an accident involving [[Wyson]] and an ultra-growth potion.]]
The [[Giant Mole]] is initially unaggressive, and will respawn in the centre of the [[Mole Hole]]. It has a basic [[melee]] attack with a max hit of 21, and no special attacks.

[[Protect from Melee]] will negate all damage. It may also be [[safespotted]] using the various rocks and cavern walls due to her size.

While between 50% and 5% of her health, every attack from the player has a 25% chance of causing her to burrow into the ground to another area in the lair, losing aggression and forcing players to chase her across the lair. {{CiteTwitter|author=Mod Ash|url=https://twitter.com/JagexAsh/status/1139454530406559744|date=14 June 2019|archiveurl=https://reldo.runescape.wiki/i/107093|archivedate=18 June 2019|quote=1/4 when its health is between 5% and 50%.}} This includes attacks that hit a 0, unless it is a magic attack that splashes. [[Poison]] damage does not cause her to burrow. Upon burrowing, there is an additional chance of her throwing dirt at the player, which extinguishes open light sources of players within melee distance, such as [[candles]] and [[torches]]. Closed sources like the [[bullseye lantern]] are unaffected.

Having a [[Falador Shield 3|Falador shield 3]] or better in your inventory will allow the player to track the location of the mole with a flashing arrow indicator. The Giant Mole must be killed at least once before this item may be obtained, as it is a reward from the hard [[Falador Diary]].

